    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d729">

                <pb facs="0727" n="627" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg627"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/7694</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Princess Cantacuzene of the
                        American Central Committee for Russian Relief</hi><anchor n="30"
                        xml:id="d729-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-11-18"><hi rendition="#italic">November 18,
                        1920</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Madam</hi>: I beg to enclose herewith, for your
                    information, a paraphrase of a telegram received from the American High
                    Commissioner at Constantinople, under date of November 15, concerning the
                    evacuation of refugees from the Crimea.<anchor n="31" xml:id="d729-f2"/></p>
                <pb facs="0728" n="628" xml:id="pg628"/>
                <p>As you are no doubt aware, the State Department has no funds available for use in
                    the alleviation of suffering among these refugees, and I am, therefore, calling
                    the matter to your attention in the hope that your organization may be able to
                    assist in taking care of these unfortunate persons.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State,<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Norman
                            H. Davis</hi></signed><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Under Secretary of
                        State</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d729-f1" n="30" type="source" xml:id="d729-f1-content">
                <p>The same on Nov. 20 to the Chairman of the American Red Cross.</p>
            </note>
